ope eCommerce, Outfitters, Third Party, Licensing, and Retail segments. It also sells uniform and logo apparel to businesses and their employees, and student households; and earns royalties on the use of Lands' End trademark. The company sells its products through its e-commerce websites and company operated stores, as well as through third party distribution channels under the Lands' End, Lands' End Lighthouse, Squall, Tugless Tank, Drifter, Outrigger, Marinac, Wanderweight, Beach Living, Supima, No-Gape, Anyweather, Waveshaper, Starfish, Little Black Suit, Iron Knees, Hyde Park, Year'Rounder, ClassMate, Willis & Geiger, and ThermaCheck brands. Lands' End, Inc. was founded in 1963 and is headquartered in Dodgeville, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charlie  Cole | CEO & Director","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $527K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Lands' End, Inc. is a micro-cap consumer cyclical business with a $267M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 43%.","The business throws off $20M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 9.01\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 72% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $58.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-58679385.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 68/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 68% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 58% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (LE) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_LE_That_Institutions_Follow_110226082201_1793625721.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793625721.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Bears Saw Before Lands' End Slid","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nasdaq-le/lands-end/news/what-bears-saw-before-lands-end-slid","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794022062.156,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.681,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Robert Galvin Acquires 1,610 Lands' End Shares at $9.51 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/robert-galvin-acquires-1610-lands-end-shares-at-951-each","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793740251.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Lands' End Announces Resignation of Head of Technology Transformation Martin Christopher","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/lands-end-announces-resignation-of-head-of-technology-transformation-martin-christopher","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793391319.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.296,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Caught Out By Lands' End's Fall? Here's What Bears Saw","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nasdaq-le/lands-end/news/caught-out-by-lands-ends-fall-heres-what-bears-saw","date":"2026-10-24","tim